The shape half of `canvas_shape_prop_read.txtar`, on the Go targets.

Separate because that one also reads a widget prop, and a widget prop read does
not compile on fyne -- `m.label.Value` against a `widget.Label` that spells it
`Text`, which predates this pass and is not what it is about. What is about it
is here: `dot.r` is answered with 5.0 and nothing in the emitted Go names the
shape, because by then `passShapeDraw` has replaced it with the calls that
paint it.

deny out/go/fyne/model.go `m\.dot\b` -- a Model field for a node that no longer exists, which is what the read used to emit
deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `m\.dot\b` -- the same on the other Go target

-- app.sngl --
import ui "sngl:ui"
import draw "sngl:ui/draw"

output {
    go {
        fyne
        bubbletea
    }
}

ui.window #w(title="shapes") {
    draw.canvas(width=100px, height=100px) {
        draw.circle #dot(cx=10.0, cy=10.0, r=5.0)
    }

    ui.text(value="r is {dot.r}")
}
